course: dictionary
lesson: 10200
title: Tinsel, shine and show
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Tinsel is long strings of thin, shiny material that glitters. People hang it on Christmas trees, and you may see it in classrooms and school plays too. You can say "a strand of tinsel" or "gold tinsel", but you cannot count it as one tinsel or two tinsels.
explain: Words can have a second meaning. Tinsel can also mean something that looks bright and exciting but has little real value. «The show was all tinsel: bright lights, but nothing inside.» The clue is "nothing inside": the show looks dazzling, but it is not worth much.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «The tree was covered in tinsel and baubles.» The words tree and baubles tell you tinsel is the shiny Christmas decoration. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Tinsel is also a word that uses the same letters as other words. «An anagram is a word made by rearranging all the letters of another word: "listen" gives "silent", "tinsel" and "enlist".» Rearranging letters is a fun puzzle, and it can help you remember words.
fact: Tinsel is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some tinsel, not one tinsel.
fact: «Tinsel» means long strings of thin, shiny material used as decoration, especially at Christmas.
fact: «Tinsel» can also mean something bright and exciting that has little real value.
fact: «Tinsel» is an anagram of «listen», «silent» and «enlist», because they use the same letters in a different order.
fact: «Tinseltown» is a nickname for Hollywood, the film capital where glamour can look dazzling.
exercise: «The tree sparkled with gold tinsel and baubles.» What is tinsel in this sentence? | A tree trunk | A kind of snow | A type of cake | *A shiny decoration
exercise: «The show was all tinsel: bright lights, but nothing inside.» What does tinsel suggest here? | Something very heavy and useful | *Something bright that has little real value | Something that is good for your health | A quiet, dark room
exercise: Which word is made from the same letters as «listen»? | glitter | shiny | garden | *silent
test: What is «Tinseltown» a nickname for? | The school hall | London | A Christmas tree farm | *Hollywood
test: Tinsel is uncountable. Which phrase is correct? | two tinsels | *some tinsel | an tinsel | a tinsel
exam: «Her necklace was tinsel, glittering but worth almost nothing.» What does tinsel mean here? | Good for keeping warm | *Bright but of little real value | Very heavy and strong | Made of solid gold
